# oracle: compute ackland/atom legacy yes (the original classification) on a displaced bcc lj crystal (3x3x3 cells, 54 atoms), 5 steps of nve; the structure of each atom is dumped at steps 0 and 5
# oracle: native: b332f28 (installed lmp; compute ackland/atom is in the EXTRA-COMPUTE package of that binary)
# oracle-files: w227xc_ackland_bcc.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none filerel=1e-12
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.9e-14, atoms n/a (atoms=none; the per-atom structure is the dump file, worst token 0).
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         bcc 1.0
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
variable        dx atom 0.15*sin(1.7*x+0.9*y-0.6*z)
variable        dy atom 0.15*cos(2.2*y-1.2*x+0.5*z)
variable        dz atom 0.15*sin(1.1*z+0.7*x-0.8*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
velocity        all create 0.6 9876 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
compute         ack all ackland/atom legacy yes
compute         ackS all reduce sum c_ack
dump            d1 all custom 5 w227xc_ackland_bcc.dump id c_ack
dump_modify     d1 sort id format float %.15g
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ke c_ackS
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             5
